,1371,1374,1375,1377,1378,1380],{},[389,1366,1354],{},": use a ",[33,1369,299],{}," function — put all logic in ",[33,1372,1373],{},"main()",", call ",[33,1376,376],{}," at the end. Keeps logic in functions (testable, reusable), avoids top-level execution (safer if ",[33,1379,532],{},"d), clear entry point.",[386,1382,1383,1385,1386,1388,1389,1392,1393,1396,1397,1400],{},[389,1384,1354],{},": use ",[33,1387,77],{}," for constants and ",[33,1390,1391],{},"local"," for function variables — ",[33,1394,1395],{},"readonly SCRIPT_DIR=..."," (catches reassignment), ",[33,1398,1399],{},"local x=0"," (function-scoped, no global pollution). Both catch common bugs.",[386,1402,1403,1367,1405,1407,1408,542,1411,1414,1415,753],{},[389,1404,1354],{},[33,1406,692],{}," function for fatal errors — ",[33,1409,1410],{},"die() { echo \"ERROR: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }",[33,1412,1413],{},"[[ -f $f ]] || die \"missing\"",". Consistent error handling, cleaner than repeated ",[33,1416,1417],{},"echo ... exit 1",[386,1419,1420,1422,1423,1426,1427,1430,1431,1433],{},[389,1421,1354],{},": keep stdout for data, stderr for messages — ",[33,1424,1425],{},"echo \"$result\""," (stdout, machine-parseable), ",[33,1428,1429],{},"echo \"Processing...\" >&2"," (stderr, human). Lets ",[33,1432,1342],{}," capture only data, logs separate.",[18,1435,1437],{"id":1436},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[383,1439,1440,1449,1476,1487,1508,1530,1553,1571,1583,1606],{},[386,1441,1442,1445,1446,1448],{},[389,1443,1444],{},"Functions must be defined before use",": Bash reads top-to-bottom. A function called before its definition fails. Put all functions first, call ",[33,1447,376],{}," at the end.",[386,1450,1451,392,1459,1461,1462,1464,1465,1467,1468,1470,1471,1473,1474,753],{},[389,1452,1453,1456,1457],{},[33,1454,1455],{},"BASH_SOURCE[0]"," vs ",[33,1458,189],{},[33,1460,189],{}," is the script name (or the shell if ",[33,1463,532],{},"d). ",[33,1466,1455],{}," is the current file's path (works in ",[